            "name": "Dinopirates from Inner Space",
            "steam_appid": 3704640,
            "required_age": 0,
            "is_free": false,
            "controller_support": "full",
            "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/cd63306b5ac997e675e8090cbc4831c4.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>TriceraTreasure Tom</strong>, a.k.a. <strong>TTT</strong>, had everything a space-faring dinosaur pirate could want: fame, fortune, his own ship (<i>Water Princess Mark II</i>), and a crew that was, admittedly, not great, but at least <i>his</i>. Life was good. Plundering was excellent. The sea shanties were tolerable.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then the <strong>Broccolites</strong> hit. Monstrous, rotting plant-creatures that consumed everything in their path, the invasion scattered TTT's crew across the Inner Space and left him adrift, broke, hungry, and forced to accept shelter aboard a rival ship.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <i>S.S. Waterqueen</i>. Captained by his oldest rival, <strong>Captain Ankylarrgh</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The position offered to TTT: <strong>janitor</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/00a01a65e3ab68bfa5a95fd38f3d2dd2.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Starting from the very bottom of the Dinopirate food chain, TTT must prove himself through increasingly dangerous, and increasingly ridiculous, missions. Each run, you battle endless hordes of <strong>Brocolites</strong> across the Inner Space, building outrageous combat loadouts from a mix of <strong>paleolithic weapons</strong> and <strong>cutting-edge dino-technology</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As your <strong>Dinopirate Level</strong> climbs, your former crewmates start paying attention again. Win back their trust. Earn your rank. And when the time is right, <strong>mutiny</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fd7ca3d78612aec31522d9eccb38684e.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fueled by the spirit of 90s action cartoons, absurd, loud, and never afraid to commit to the bit, <i>Dinopirates from Inner Space</i> blends fast-paced roguelike gameplay with a story that somehow makes you root for a disgraced dinosaur janitor fighting his way back to pirate captaincy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Top-down action roguelike with deep build customization every run</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb the <strong>Dinopirate hierarchy</strong> from janitor to captain</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Wild weapon combos: bone clubs meet plasma cannons, paleolithic meets dino-tech</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rescue defenseless <strong>Crew Members</strong> scattered across the Inner Space</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Permanent upgrades</strong> and progression between runs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A universe built on <strong>absurd humor</strong> with genuine narrative stakes</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Wishlist on Steam — the mop can only hold TTT back for so long.</strong></p>",
            "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/cd63306b5ac997e675e8090cbc4831c4.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/0fab046e5972ca0ba52259698ba7cd95.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>TriceraTreasure Tom</strong>, a.k.a. <strong>TTT</strong>, had everything a space-faring dinosaur pirate could want: fame, fortune, his own ship (<i>Water Princess Mark II</i>), and a crew that was, admittedly, not great, but at least <i>his</i>. Life was good. Plundering was excellent. The sea shanties were tolerable.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Then the <strong>Broccolites</strong> hit. Monstrous, rotting plant-creatures that consumed everything in their path, the invasion scattered TTT's crew across the Inner Space and left him adrift, broke, hungry, and forced to accept shelter aboard a rival ship.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The <i>S.S. Waterqueen</i>. Captained by his oldest rival, <strong>Captain Ankylarrgh</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The position offered to TTT: <strong>janitor</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/00a01a65e3ab68bfa5a95fd38f3d2dd2.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fbdbd86bc133b3f9c695caa7a10b37d3.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Starting from the very bottom of the Dinopirate food chain, TTT must prove himself through increasingly dangerous, and increasingly ridiculous, missions. Each run, you battle endless hordes of <strong>Brocolites</strong> across the Inner Space, building outrageous combat loadouts from a mix of <strong>paleolithic weapons</strong> and <strong>cutting-edge dino-technology</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As your <strong>Dinopirate Level</strong> climbs, your former crewmates start paying attention again. Win back their trust. Earn your rank. And when the time is right, <strong>mutiny</strong>.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/fd7ca3d78612aec31522d9eccb38684e.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1560 height=171 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.poster.avif?t=1785465717\" width=1170 height=304 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.webm?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3704640/extras/8761abaa4c5389dd20032b6c4b550195.mp4?t=1785465717\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Fueled by the spirit of 90s action cartoons, absurd, loud, and never afraid to commit to the bit, <i>Dinopirates from Inner Space</i> blends fast-paced roguelike gameplay with a story that somehow makes you root for a disgraced dinosaur janitor fighting his way back to pirate captaincy.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Key Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Top-down action roguelike with deep build customization every run</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Climb the <strong>Dinopirate hierarchy</strong> from janitor to captain</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Wild weapon combos: bone clubs meet plasma cannons, paleolithic meets dino-tech</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rescue defenseless <strong>Crew Members</strong> scattered across the Inner Space</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Permanent upgrades</strong> and progression between runs</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A universe built on <strong>absurd humor</strong> with genuine narrative stakes</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Wishlist on Steam — the mop can only hold TTT back for so long.</strong></p>",
            "short_description": "An action roguelike set in sci-fi space where dinosaurs, dino-tech weapons, and chaos collide. Reclaim your honor as Captain TTT, fight deadly Brocolites, rescue your crew, and conquer the Inner Space.",
